# Build-context exclusions.
#
# READ THIS BEFORE ADDING A PATTERN (#310): .dockerignore is NOT .gitignore.
# Docker matches each pattern against the whole relative path with Go's
# filepath.Match semantics, so a pattern with no leading `**/` is anchored at the
# CONTEXT ROOT. Plain `__pycache__/` therefore only ever matched
# backend/__pycache__, and every nested bytecode dir (app/**, migrations/**)
# shipped in the image as stale host bytecode. Anything that can appear at any
# depth needs the `**/` prefix; `**/x` matches `x` at the root too.

# Host bytecode + tool caches (host tags never match the image interpreter).
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache

# Local databases — the dev app DB and any sample source DB. Never bake one in.
**/*.db
**/*.sqlite
**/*.duckdb

# Secrets are kept out of the CONTEXT, not merely out of a COPY: the whole
# context is uploaded to the daemon (possibly remote) before any COPY runs.
**/.env

# Root-anchored ON PURPOSE: this is backend/tests, the only test tree in this
# context. `**/tests` would also swallow a tests/ dir inside anything vendored
# under backend/ later.
tests/
